{
  "_meta": {
    "created": "2026-07-22",
    "purpose": "Human-audited ground truth for the doorway-notch suppression risk surface (reports/p3a-notch-resolution.md). Oracle for gate_flip_check_audited.py -- NOT classify()'s output. classify() is the CANDIDATE GENERATOR (finds edges to audit); this file is the audited verdict.",
    "scope": "Every a_genuine_gt_defect_between_rooms edge (classify()'s pre-fix output) with opening_coverage >= 0.65, exhaustively enumerated across the full 17,000-plan ResPlan population as of this date. This is the ONLY band check_plan's suppression predicate can ever touch (opening_cov >= 0.65 is one of its three conjuncts), so it bounds the entire false-suppression risk surface.",
    "regeneration_trigger": "Any new a_genuine_gt_defect_between_rooms edge with opening_coverage >= 0.65 that appears after GT growth (new plans added to ResPlan, or classify()'s upstream signals change) is NOT covered by this file and must be manually audited (rendered + visually verified) before being trusted by the gate. gate_flip_check_audited.py checks for and flags any such edge by (plan_id, room, edge_index) key not present here.",
    "updated_2026_07_26": "Added 57 previously-UNAUDITED edges (priority 1 of the next-session spec in reports/p3a-notch-resolution.md). All 57 confirmed NOT a doorway notch by visual audit -- classify()'s exclusion of them from e_opening_doorway_notch is correct in every case (0/57 wrongly excluded). Dominant mechanism (not_notch_diagonal_wall_mismatch, ~46/57): a smooth diagonal room-boundary edge over a wall the source represents as an axis-aligned staircase, or absent from the wall polygon's own edge set at that angle -- real wall ink is visibly present in every overlay; this is a coverage-matching TECHNIQUE limitation, not evidence of an omitted partition. See reports/p3a-audit-57-unaudited.md for the full per-edge rationale and the duplicate-edge/duplicate-plan findings."
  },
